# shadcn/ui Component Library — MANDATORY

This project uses **shadcn/ui** as the **sole** UI component library. This is non-negotiable.

> **ZERO custom UI components.** Do not write custom HTML elements, raw CSS components, inline styles, or Tailwind utility soup that recreates a component shadcn/ui already provides. If shadcn/ui has it, use it — no exceptions.

## Initialization

If shadcn/ui is not yet initialized in the project, run:

```bash
npx shadcn@latest init
```

## Adding Components

If a required component is not yet installed, add it before using it:

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add <component-name>
```

Examples:
```bash
npx shadcn@latest add button
npx shadcn@latest add input
npx shadcn@latest add dialog
```

## Clerk Authentication UI

All Clerk sign-in and sign-up entry points **must** follow these rules:

1. **Use shadcn/ui `<Button>`** — never render Clerk's built-in `<SignInButton>` or `<SignUpButton>` with custom HTML. Wrap them so the trigger is always a shadcn/ui `<Button>`.
2. **Modal mode only** — Clerk must be configured to open sign-in and sign-up inside a modal, never as a full-page redirect or an embedded inline form. Pass `mode="modal"` to `<SignInButton>` and `<SignUpButton>`.

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT — shadcn Button trigger + modal mode
import { SignInButton, SignUpButton } from '@clerk/nextjs';
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button';

<SignInButton mode="modal">
  <Button variant="outline">Sign in</Button>
</SignInButton>

<SignUpButton mode="modal">
  <Button>Get started</Button>
</SignUpButton>

// ❌ WRONG — raw HTML trigger
<SignInButton>
  <button className="my-custom-btn">Sign in</button>
</SignInButton>

// ❌ WRONG — full-page redirect (no mode prop or mode="redirect")
<SignInButton mode="redirect">
  <Button>Sign in</Button>
</SignInButton>
```

## Hard Rules

- **No custom components.** Never create a bespoke button, input, card, dialog, badge, avatar, dropdown, or any other element that duplicates shadcn/ui functionality.
- **No raw HTML for UI.** `<div>`, `<button>`, `<input>`, etc. are only acceptable inside shadcn/ui component implementations themselves — never in application code where a shadcn/ui primitive exists.
- **No other component libraries.** Do not install or use MUI, Chakra, Radix primitives directly, Headless UI, Ant Design, or any other UI library alongside shadcn/ui.
- Always check `components/ui/` before assuming a component is available.
- Import components from `@/components/ui/<component>`.
- Run the `add` command for any component not yet present in `components/ui/`.
- This project is in dark mode so make sure there are no dark colored text on dark backgrounds (and vice versa).
